objectives.text:
Pupils should be able to:
1. enumerate the uses of money;
2. recognize all types of Nigerian coins and bank notes;
3. change money up to ₦20 into small units and shop with money not greater than ₦20.

Pupils should be able to:
1.  compare their natural units with another e.g. arm‟s length;
2. identify the differences in arm‟s length and other parts of the body used for measurement;
3.  use meters and centimetres as standard measuring units;
4. identify the need for lengths and measurement using standardized units.

Pupils should be able to:
1. give time to the hour and half;
2. name and arrange days of the week.
